Hi, I'm a research assistant and a PhD student at Senckenberg Society for Nature Research in Deep-Sea Benthic Biology. My work focuses on taxonomy, biogeography, and ecology of the benthic peracarid crustaceans. 

I am currently starting my PhD, although I can't elaborate the topics in detail here, there are still something to share. First, it will be something about networks in the deep-sea benthos, and second, it will involve a new isopod family previously unknown to science currently described by me and my collegue. It's still in the stage of actively developing the ideas into plans. 

In the meantime, I am strongly associated with [ALONGate Project](https://zzzhehao.github.io/ALONGate_Project/) and the evaluation of [Deep Arctic Expedition](https://act.greenpeace.de/deep-arctic-expedition). I support both projects with my expertises in various fields:

- On-site support for planning and operation of ROV biological surveys, benthic sample collection
- Identification and DNA barcoding of the collected samples
- Description of species new to science
- Maintaining databases for samples and imaging data
- Biodiversity assessments 
- Public outreach (have a look at our [ALONGate website](https://zzzhehao.github.io/ALONGate_Project/)!)

